      "message": "\u003e it would be better to change that and return 2 values, an error code and the token if error code \u003d\u003d 0.\n\nThis is exactly what `Result\u003cu64\u003e` means 😊\n\n\u003e Regarding the size, currently, the function must pass the range as seen in the device tree\n\nAck so that must be documented here.\n\n\u003e If we have a resource less than that, so this device can\u0027t be assigned.\n\nBut aren\u0027t there cases where the MMIO is isolated in its own page (so assignable) or assigned as a group with all the other devices in said page but doesn\u0027t cover the whole page? In that case `\u003creg\u003e` would contain less than `PAGE_SIZE` (as the guest driver doesn\u0027t need/shouldn\u0027t get more) but should still be verifiable through this interface, no?",
