      "writtenOn": "2023-11-20T17:55:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Ah, I said function but I meant the HVC.\n\nI see; why don\u0027t you want to use the SMCCC `R0` result? Negative values/the sign bit?\n\n\u003e Do you mean that 2 VMs or host and a VM would share part of a page of the MMIO of the device?\n\nNo, I meant assigning **to the same pVM** `devA` alone when (host DT)\n```\n/{\n    devA@0x1000 { reg \u003d \u003c0x1000 0x800\u003e };\n    // nothing else uses page 0x1000\n}\n```\nor `devA` and `devB` when\n```\n/{\n    devA@0x1000 { reg \u003d \u003c0x1000 0x800\u003e };\n    devB@0x1800 { reg \u003d \u003c0x1800 0x800\u003e };\n}\n```\nwhich are both valid assignments AFAICT and would result in (resp.) the HVCs\n```\nrequest_mmio(0x1000, 0x800);\n```\nand\n```\nrequest_mmio(0x1000, 0x800);\nrequest_mmio(0x1800, 0x800);\n```\nall of which would (incorrectly, IMO) fail if `size` (or even `base_ipa`) had to be page-aligned?",
      "parentUuid": "f7ff50d9_e9be50ec",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 83,
        "startChar": 46,
        "endLine": 83,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "2eae56d633800d37681ef2fca25b44d180a51a4f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "94f86720_f990c22e",
        "filename": "libs/hyp/src/hypervisor/common.rs",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 83,
      "author": {
        "id": 1965911
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-20T18:08:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I see; why don\u0027t you want to use the SMCCC R0 result? Negative values/the sign bit?\n\nThat\u0027s what is done now, (in the link I sent above)\n\n\u003e all of which would (incorrectly, IMO) fail if size (or even base_ipa) had to be page-aligned?\n\nYes, that would fail, no just the `request_mmio` but pKVM will reject registering this device as assignable, as it can\u0027t isolate it.\n\nI believe the best solution for this is to make `regs` `PAGE_SIZE` aligned and the driver would ignore the rest of the MMIO.\n\nI am not sure if there is any case like this exists, typically in Linux the driver would `ioremap` the MMIO of a device which must be done with `PAGE_SIZE` alignment, so the driver must understand the last `0x800` are not usable.\n\nFor the second case, I guess they would be described as one device, as each one can\u0027t be isolated separately.",
      "parentUuid": "0454a386_ded34420",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 83,
        "startChar": 46,
        "endLine": 83,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "2eae56d633800d37681ef2fca25b44d180a51a4f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "18d1fdb9_0fa66843",
        "filename": "libs/hyp/src/hypervisor/common.rs",
        "patchSetId": 12
