      "writtenOn": "2023-11-20T18:34:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e That\u0027s what is done now, (in the link I sent above)\n\nAck; I thought you were adding more details and had missed that you were actually correcting yourself.\n\n\u003e I believe the best solution for this is to make `regs` `PAGE_SIZE` aligned and the driver would ignore the rest of the MMIO. [...] For the second case, I guess they would be described as one device, as each one can\u0027t be isolated separately.\n\nRight; I feel like this is conflating driver binding with \"assignability\". The former, either happening in the guest or host, should only use `\u003creg\u003e` (not more) and have no dependency on `PAGE_SIZE` (hidden behind `ioremap`, as you said), while only assignment (to VMs or even regular VFIO) does.\n\nI guess this isn\u0027t something we\u0027re addressing here but I wonder if a cleaner sub-page registration of the `\"pkvm,device-assignment\"` nodes would be possible, to support the calls I\u0027m describing above, which could be added later in a backward-compatible way AFAICT.\n\n\u003e I am not sure if there is any case like this exists\n\nMany results of `rgrep \u0027reg \u003d\u0027 arch/arm64/boot/dts/` aren\u0027t 4KiB-aligned in size.",
      "parentUuid": "94f86720_f990c22e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 83,
        "startChar": 46,
        "endLine": 83,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "2eae56d633800d37681ef2fca25b44d180a51a4f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "75cd7986_97624e7a",
        "filename": "libs/hyp/src/hypervisor/common.rs",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 83,
      "author": {
        "id": 1965911
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-20T18:58:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Many results of rgrep \u0027reg \u003d\u0027 arch/arm64/boot/dts/ aren\u0027t 4KiB-aligned in size.\n\nDoes any of these actually have the rest of the page free but are described with less than that, so they are assignable by HW but would be rejected by pKVM?\n\nI am not sure how we can address this, for example VFIO will not allow mapping devices to user space if they are not aligned to `PAGE_SIZE`[1], I think it is a valid requirement, and pKVM should reject assignment if the device is not aligned and for devices that need to do so, they should fix their device tree.\n\nOne other approach would be to allow any device to be registered for assignment and pKVM would unmap the MMIO from the host with `PAGE_SIZE` alignment when the device is assigned, however I don\u0027t like that as it is less transparent.\n\n[1] https://elixir.bootlin.com/linux/v6.2/source/drivers/vfio/platform/vfio_platform_common.c#L169",
      "parentUuid": "18d1fdb9_0fa66843",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 83,
        "startChar": 46,
        "endLine": 83,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "2eae56d633800d37681ef2fca25b44d180a51a4f",
