      "writtenOn": "2023-11-20T19:21:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay, thanks for the pointers; so as long as [1] exists, we won\u0027t have a uAPI to assign devices with sub-page granularity anyway, even if it might make sense in some particular cases.\n\nKeeping this comment thread open for @jaewan@google.com to document these points, as we\u0027ll need to validate these assumptions when pvmfw gets extended to DA on other hypervisors i.e. the hypervisor rejects misaligned `base_ipa` \u0026 `size` (remember that `PAGE_SIZE` might not be 4KiB!) or `size` not covering the whole region and, on success, the result is a _token_, not a PA (pKVM currently having token\u003d\u003dPA is an implementation detail).\n\nAlso, can we rename the method to something more descriptive such as `get_phys_mmio_token`, because it currently sounds like it\u0027s requesting the actual MMIO assignment to be performed? Similarly, `get_phys_iommu_token` below?",
